<ROSETTASCRIPTS>
    <!--
        fastrelax_for_ia.xml
        ────────────────────
        FastRelax pre-treatment for InterfaceAnalyzer ΔΔG scoring of
        predicted protein-protein complexes.

        One Cartesian-space FastRelax repeat with the ref2015 score
        function.  This is the canonical setup used in Bennett et al.
        2023 for de novo binder ΔΔG calibration, so the resulting
        rosetta_ddg values are directly comparable to that paper's
        −30 REU threshold.

        Why one repeat, why Cartesian, why ref2015_cart:

          - default_repeats=1 captures the bulk of the energy
            improvement (clash relief, sidechain optimisation) at
            ~3-6 min wall time per ~150-residue complex.  Additional
            repeats give diminishing returns.
          - cartesian=true minimises in Cartesian coordinates rather
            than torsion space, which is more robust on predicted
            structures whose bond geometry may differ slightly from
            ideal (Boltz/AlphaFold/etc do not enforce strict
            stereochemistry).
          - ref2015_cart adds the cart_bonded term that penalises
            bond-length and bond-angle deviation, which Cartesian
            minimisation needs to avoid drifting toward unphysical
            geometries.

        No constraints, no fixed regions: the entire complex relaxes
        as one body so both bound-state energy AND inter-chain
        geometry are simultaneously optimised.  InterfaceAnalyzer
        then computes the unbound state by chain separation +
        repacking.
    -->

    <SCOREFXNS>
        <ScoreFunction name="r15_cart" weights="ref2015_cart"/>
    </SCOREFXNS>

    <MOVERS>
        <!--
            FastRelax in this Rosetta build (2025.37) does not accept
            'default_repeats' as an XML attribute — that setting must
            be passed as the command-line option '-relax:default_repeats'
            instead.  See run_rosetta_metrics.py:_run_fast_relax for
            where the option is added to the rosetta_scripts cmdline.
        -->
        <FastRelax name="relax"
                   scorefxn="r15_cart"
                   cartesian="true"/>
    </MOVERS>

    <PROTOCOLS>
        <Add mover="relax"/>
    </PROTOCOLS>

    <OUTPUT scorefxn="r15_cart"/>

</ROSETTASCRIPTS>